# Forward-Only Changes (No Legacy Compatibility)

For this repository, prefer forward-only evolution over compatibility shims.

## Rule

- Do not add backward-compatibility flags, aliases, deprecated code paths, or dual APIs.
- When replacing an API/config option, remove the old form in the same change.
- Update call sites to the new API instead of keeping translation layers.
- If migration is needed, do it directly in-repo (single active path), not via legacy fallbacks.
- When any public API/config/CLI behavior changes, update all relevant docs in the same change.
- Relevant docs include (at minimum): inline usage comments near the API, README/bridge docs that show usage, and any skills/rules that reference the old API.
- A change is not complete until code and docs reflect the same current API.

## Current example

- Use `debug_color: :off | :sides | :components_reuse`.
- Do not reintroduce `debug_paint_faces` or `debug_component_reuse_colors`.
